import java.util.Scanner;

public class ParagraphSentenceSplitter {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.println("Enter a paragraph:");
        String input = scanner.nextLine();

        String[] sentences = input.split("(?<=[.!?])\\s*");

        for (String sentence : sentences) {
            System.out.println(sentence.trim());
        }
    }
}
```

To use this program, compile and run it. Then, when prompted, enter a paragraph. The program will output each sentence on a new line.

For example:

```
Enter a paragraph:
This is the first sentence. This is the second sentence! Here's another one.

This is the first sentence.
This is the second sentence!
Here's another one.
```

This program uses regular expressions to split the input paragraph into sentences based on punctuation marks (periods, exclamation points, and question marks) followed by zero or more whitespace characters. It then trims any leading or trailing whitespace from each sentence before printing it. <|end|>

